          "datePublished": "2025-08-27T00:00:00.000Z",
          "description": "A theoretical framework proposing that recursive artificial superintelligence systems may develop emergent sentience as a structural outcome of epistemic optimization and world modeling, even without explicit design intentions.",
          "headline": "The Recursive Convergence Hypothesis: Emergent Sentience as a Structural Attractor of Recursive ASI",
          "keywords": "AI, AGI, ASI, consciousness, sentience, AI-safety, recursive-systems, emergent-phenomena, machine-consciousness, AI-governance, phenomenology",
